cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, the generated annotations, or build on this work,
  please cite the accompanying paper (see "preferred-citation") as well as this
  repository.
title: >-
  Fault Inception Detection in Real-World Disturbance Data for Power System
  Protection
abstract: >-
  Training-free, physics-guided reference implementation for estimating fault
  inception timestamps (t0) in real-world transmission disturbance recordings.
  The method combines protection-domain indicators, robust median/MAD-based
  normalization, a low-latency transient path, and persistence-aware fusion and
  veto logic to distinguish fault-consistent disturbances from non-fault
  transients such as switching, energization, resonance, and measurement
  artifacts.
type: software
license: BSD-3-Clause
